  "report": "Initial stage: packaging receives repeated positive comments in one brand-owned TikTok thread, especially aesthetic approval (P00, P38, P40), broader packaging appreciation (P21, P26, P39), and excitement about refillability (P42). These support favorable reception among the commenting accounts, not verified performance or representative customer sentiment. P00’s combined chic/environmentally friendly statement has 296 displayed likes; P15’s proposed empty-container reuse has 150. These are conspicuous audience resonance, not independent experiences. Other focal comments have 0–12 likes except the brand’s P01 agreement (39). Environmental benefit and recyclability remain unverified: P02 questions them, P03 offers qualified speculation, and P01 is brand agreement. P03 is the same actor as P00, not independent corroboration.\n\nFailure and remedy: P06 alone reports arrival leakage with a loose top, opening and cleaning the package, and concern about oxygen exposure. SKU and version are unknown; thread placement cannot identify them. Its 12 likes do not establish additional leaks. P07, the brand response with 12 likes, says short-term exposure is not an issue and offers a replacement through email. This establishes an offer and brand reassurance, not independent safety verification, a replacement sent, delivery, or successful resolution. No supplied focal account provides bare arrival agreement, a second leak experience, or retailer leakage. The loose-top report does not establish a general causal mechanism or defect rate.\n\nConsequences: P17 reports an all-Experiment routine and Continuum in the mail, explicitly describing unusual brand loyalty. P20 declares broad buying enthusiasm without completed checkout evidence. P32 expresses tentative saving/purchase interest; P38 anticipates trying the product. P42 reports receipt that day and newly discovered refillability, so refill awareness cannot be credited as the stated reason for that acquisition. P04 requests refill bundles; P27 specifically requests a Continuum/Super Saturated refill bundle. Neither establishes repeat purchase intent or action. P15 proposes reuse for Lexapro storage, not completed reuse or demonstrated suitability. P29 asks about getting the sticker in their refill. None explicitly attributes a completed purchase, repurchase, switching, or abandonment to packaging. Praise and a service complaint coexist at thread level; the complaining actor does not state loyalty or abandonment.\n\nConflict and limits: reception is mixed across appreciation, environmental skepticism, a skin-benefit question, and an arrival defect, but these concern different propositions and do not directly refute one another. No opposing leak outcome is supplied. Product/version scope is generally unknown; named products in P17/P27 cannot donate scope to neighboring comments. All focal evidence is from one TikTok thread, with no cross-venue corroboration. Context records are empty. The supplied capture reports 47 displayed bodies versus 72 advertised comments, with only selected reply branches expanded; the 19 focal records are not a complete population. Native comment IDs are unavailable. Displayed dates are month-day without a year; engagement was observed on 2026-09-09. Counts below count qualifying focal source accounts, not independent people or events; zeros mean none in the supplied focal set. No second-stage source accounts or context were supplied, so second-stage findings, changes, and counts cannot be diagnosed.",
  "source_index": [
    {
      "key": "P00",
      "findings": "@randomdude7551, TikTok 5-15, 296 likes: calls metal packaging chic and environmentally friendly. Strong visible resonance for the bundled opinion; environmental performance unverified, SKU/version unknown. Same actor as P03."
    },
    {
      "key": "P01",
      "findings": "@experimentwrld, brand/creator reply to P00, 5-15, 39 likes: agrees completely. Owned endorsement, not independent customer or environmental corroboration; same brand actor as P07."
    },
    {
      "key": "P02",
      "findings": "@person1234567556987, reply to P00, 5-15, 0 likes: questions environmental friendliness and recyclability. Unresolved challenge, not evidence that packaging is unrecyclable."
    },
    {
      "key": "P03",
      "findings": "@randomdude7551, reply under P00, 5-15, 2 likes: says aluminum is almost always recyclable, inner part likely recyclable, pump likely not, and pump/shell reusable. Qualified assertions without verification; same origin as P00, SKU/version unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P04",
      "findings": "@flamingpanda5, reply under P00, 5-20, 0 likes: requests refill bundles. Product unspecified; request does not establish purchase or repurchase intent."
    },
    {
      "key": "P06",
      "findings": "@jasminesingh1102, 5-15, 12 likes: reports product arriving leaked with loose top, opening/cleaning it and concern about oxygen exposure and usability. One detailed arrival-leak/loose-top account; SKU/version, actual damage, later use and remedy outcome unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P07",
      "findings": "@experimentwrld, brand reply to P06, 5-16, 12 likes: says short-term exposure is not an issue and offers a replacement if customer emails hey@experimentbeauty.com. Offer only; dispatch, receipt and resolution unconfirmed; reassurance is brand testimony."
    },
    {
      "key": "P15",
      "findings": "@bmdubs, 5-15, 150 likes: intends to use their empty container for Lexapro. Resonance for proposed reuse; completed reuse and medication-storage suitability unestablished, SKU unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P17",
      "findings": "@mostlyconceptual, 5-16, 1 like: reports an all-Experiment skincare routine despite previously lacking brand loyalty, with Continuum in the mail. Explicit loyalty and shipment report; no packaging attribution, delivery confirmation, or repeat-purchase intent."
    },
    {
      "key": "P20",
      "findings": "@countryboiiloveyouuuxoxo, 5-15, 7 likes: says they are buying everything from the brand. Broad buying declaration; specific products, completed checkout and packaging motivation unconfirmed."
    },
    {
      "key": "P21",
      "findings": "@beautybought, 5-17, 1 like: praises consistently good products and packaging they can feel good about. Broad appreciation, not verified sustainability or a narrated buying consequence."
    },
    {
      "key": "P26",
      "findings": "@adam_thomas6, 5-21, 1 like: calls packaging great but asks what the product does for skin. Packaging approval alongside unresolved efficacy interest, not a negative skin-outcome report."
    },
    {
      "key": "P27",
      "findings": "@sofieeee120, 5-24, 1 like: asks for a bundle of Continuum and Super Saturated refills. Named-product bundle interest, without purchase, joint-use or explicit repurchase evidence."
    },
    {
      "key": "P29",
      "findings": "@allthegr8namesaretaken, 5-17, 2 likes: asks how to get the sticker in their refill. Preserves a sticker/refill question; exact intended operation, SKU and buying consequence unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P32",
      "findings": "@josemarbp, 5-18, 3 likes: calls the referenced offering genius and says they might save up for it. Tentative purchase interest with saving mentioned; precise referent and completed action unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P38",
      "findings": "@taylorelissa, 5-16, 1 like: calls package cute and anticipates trying it. Aesthetic approval and trial interest, not verified use or purchase; SKU unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P39",
      "findings": "@morco11111, 5-29, 1 like: appreciates the brand taking packaging as seriously as formulas. General packaging approval, without measured performance or buying consequence."
    },
    {
      "key": "P40",
      "findings": "@danaisabellaaa, 5-15, 1 like: calls the referent very cute. Contextual aesthetic approval; exact product and experience unestablished."
    },
    {
      "key": "P42",
      "findings": "@__whitneyjade, 5-20, 1 like: reports receiving theirs that day and excitement at learning it is refillable. Receipt plus newly acquired refill awareness; SKU unknown, no refill purchase or packaging-driven acquisition established."
    }
  ],
